343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 115 0 R
/T (Traditional biomechanical and physiological monitoring methods suffer from substantial technological and practical limitations. High-precision optical motion capture systems \(e.g., multi-camera infrared rigs\) require dedicated indoor laboratory spaces, complex calibration routines, and prohibitive equipment investments exceeding tens of thousands of dollars. Similarly, metabolic monitoring equipment is bulky, preventing natural movement during real-world tasks. )
