/T (Biomedical and Ergonomic Digital Twins: The concept of the digital twin has evolved from structural aerospace health monitoring to complex biological systems. Tao et al. [1] established fundamental architectural requirements for cyber-physical twin synchronization, identifying physical-to-virtual latency as the primary constraint on digital twin fidelity. In biomedical contexts, Al-Masri et al. [4] investigated cloud-hosted physiological simulators, demonstrating that integrating real-time telemetry into computational models enables predictive diagnostics for systemic fatigue and cardiovascular anomalies. )
/E (Biomedical and Ergonomic Digital Twins: The concept of the digital twin has evolved from structural aerospace health monitoring to complex biological systems. Tao et al. [1] established fundamental architectural requirements for cyber-physical twin synchronization, identifying physical-to-virtual latency as the primary constraint on digital twin fidelity. In biomedical contexts, Al-Masri et al. [4] investigated cloud-hosted physiological simulators, demonstrating that integrating real-time telemetry into computational models enables predictive diagnostics for systemic fatigue and cardiovascular anomalies. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
