/T (The Human Body Digital Twin Simulator successfully demonstrates a cost-effective, high-precision cyber- physical framework bridging physical human telemetry with real-time computational biomechanics. By integrating ESP32 edge processing nodes, 9-DOF inertial sensing, PPG pulse oximetry, surface electromyography, and high-performance WebGL 3D rendering engines, the system achieves sub-35 ms synchronization latency with high kinematic tracking accuracy \(>97.2%\). )
/E (The Human Body Digital Twin Simulator successfully demonstrates a cost-effective, high-precision cyber- physical framework bridging physical human telemetry with real-time computational biomechanics. By integrating ESP32 edge processing nodes, 9-DOF inertial sensing, PPG pulse oximetry, surface electromyography, and high-performance WebGL 3D rendering engines, the system achieves sub-35 ms synchronization latency with high kinematic tracking accuracy \(>97.2%\). )
